cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "photoncount: a photon-counting optical receiver chain for photon-starved optical links"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Poisson counting statistics for a photon-counting receiver; the Webb
  approximation for avalanche-photodiode excess-noise counting statistics, with
  its closed-form first three moments derived and verified here and its Gaussian
  and Poisson limits measured rather than asserted; M-ary pulse-position
  modulation slot statistics with an exact hard-decision symbol error
  probability, the Poisson-channel per-slot log-likelihood derived in closed
  form, symbol posteriors and bit log-likelihood ratios; paralyzable and
  non-paralyzable dead time with both forward relations, both inverse branches
  through the Lambert W function, and the non-monotonicity of the paralyzable
  map treated as a first-class hazard; afterpulsing as a Poisson cluster process
  with closed-form cluster moments and Fano factors and its suppression by dead
  time; erasure-channel capacity, hard-decision capacity, a Monte Carlo
  soft-decision achievable rate and the PPM photons-per-bit limit; an
  event-level detector simulator used as ground truth; a hardware abstraction
  layer with one contract, a simulated backend, a device stub that refuses, and
  one shared contract test suite; preflight, capture and backout procedures as
  executable checks; and a learned incident-rate correction with a quantile
  uncertainty interval, benchmarked against the closed-form inversions
  implemented first. Validation level 3, hardware-pending: no number in this
  repository came from a photon-counting detector or from a
  flight-representative board. Research grade. Not flight-qualified, not
  certified, not approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - photon-counting
  - pulse-position-modulation
  - poisson-channel
  - deep-space-optical-communications
  - avalanche-photodiode
  - webb-distribution
  - dead-time
  - afterpulsing
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Webb
        given-names: "P. P."
      - family-names: McIntyre
        given-names: "R. J."
      - family-names: Conradi
        given-names: J.
    title: "Properties of avalanche photodiodes"
    journal: "RCA Review"
    volume: 35
    issue: 2
    start: 234
    end: 278
    year: 1974
    notes: >-
      Source of the Webb approximation implemented in photoncount.webb. The
      volume, year and start page were confirmed from two independent reference
      lists citing the paper on 2026-10-06. This repository does not quote a
      page number from the paper itself and derives the moment expressions of
      the distribution numerically rather than taking them from the text.
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Knoll
        given-names: "Glenn F."
    title: "Radiation Detection and Measurement"
    edition: "4th"
    publisher:
      name: "John Wiley & Sons"
    year: 2010
    notes: >-
      Chapter 4 covers the paralyzable and non-paralyzable dead-time models
      implemented in photoncount.deadtime. No page number is quoted; the
      relations are standard and are re-derived and verified in
      validation/validate_deadtime.py.
  - type: report
    authors:
      - family-names: Hamkins
        given-names: J.
      - family-names: Moision
        given-names: B.
    title: "Multipulse Pulse-Position Modulation on Discrete Memoryless Channels"
    institution:
      name: "Jet Propulsion Laboratory"
    number: "IPN Progress Report 42-161"
    year: 2005
    month: 5
    notes: >-
      The deep-space PPM context for photoncount.ppm. Title, authors, report
      number and date of 15 May 2005 were read from the JPL IPN Progress Report
      index on 2026-10-06. This repository implements the single-pulse M-ary
      case and takes no numerical result from the report.
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Gagliardi
        given-names: "Robert M."
      - family-names: Karp
        given-names: Sherman
    title: "Optical Communications"
    edition: "2nd"
    publisher:
      name: "John Wiley & Sons"
    year: 1995
    isbn: "9780471542872"
    notes: >-
      The semiclassical photon-counting receiver model behind photoncount.poisson.
      The ISBN was confirmed from the publisher's listing on 2026-10-06. No page
      number is quoted.
